"""Abo Fles topic data — the single source of truth for domains, areas, topics, tiers and signals.

Read by scripts/gen_matrix.py (which generates topics.md, topic-index.md, matrix.md, workflow.md and
hooks/workflow.json) — never by the model: the skill looks a topic up with `scripts/topic.py find "<ask>"`.

DOMAINS = [(code, name, blurb, {3: [reviewers], 4: [reviewers]}, [(area, [topic lines])])]

Topic line: "Name | T# | signal, signal, …[ | ov Side=model·effort[,Side=…]][ | cap Side=N[,Side=N]][ | +reviewer[,+reviewer]]"
  - T# = the tier a mistake there costs (1 cosmetic · 2 a test catches it · 3 wrong prod behaviour or business rule · 4 money, auth, data loss, breach, irreversible)
  - signals = words in the ask that point here (names, aliases, tools, abbreviations); the lookup scores them
  - ov = cell overrides of the tier base; cap = reply-cap overrides; +reviewer = always added at T3/T4 (compliance, finance, security, tester, qa, uiux, cleancoder)
Topic names are unique across the file. Names used by the hook, tests or docs (the first 100) must keep their exact spelling.
"""

